violet: FYI the new Next Starter (LangChain + LlamaIndex wiring) is flaking our eval harness intermittently. Minimal repro below.

andre: Symptoms? 401s or stream truncation?

morgan: Mostly 401 during token rotation, then the SDK retries but the retry sometimes uses the old token -> partial output. Harness reports truncated text.

violet: Example handler in the starter:```js
export const runtime = 'edge';
export default async function handler(req) {
  const { q } = await req.json();
  const r = await fetch(`${process.env.REDWOOD_BASE}/v1/chat`, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_KEY}` },
    body: JSON.stringify({ input: q })
  });
  return new Response(await r.text(), { status: r.status });
}
```

andre: Two easy fixes: bump the SDK in the template to the patch with the refresh concurrency fix, and add an explicit guard that errors clearly if the env key is missing in edge.

morgan: Agree. Also add a tiny msw unit test that simulates token expiry: first /v1/chat => 401, token refresh => 200, retry chat => 200 full stream. That would've caught it. Keep the test fast.

violet: On the harness side can we treat 401 as potentially transient during rotation? Retry with small exponential backoff up to 3 attempts before marking failure. Right now any non-200 fails the run.

andre: Yep — change is low-risk and mirrors real deployment behavior.

morgan: I'll open a PR in the starter: bump @redwood/sdk -> 0.12.3, add top-of-handler guard:```js
if (!process.env.REDWOOD_KEY) throw new Error('REDWOOD_KEY missing; set .env.local or use server runtime');
```

violet: Please also add a short README note "Edge runtime gotchas" and the guard snippet so new users don't hit this during quickstart.

ci-bot: Created issue #3771: "next-starter: token refresh race in edge runtime causes intermittent 401 & truncated eval output" assigned to morgan  https://issues.redwood/3771

devex-bot: PR created: examples/next-starter#210 - bump sdk; add env guard; add msw test. CI pending.

andre: After merge QA should re-run the harness and unflag the flaky job. Small DX fixes, big payoff. :sparkles:
